-- title:
--   Vanishing at all truncated points gives membership in I(y)
-- statement:
--   Let $B$ be a commutative ring, let $I$ be a finitely generated ideal of the two-variable power series ring $B[\![x_1,x_2]\!]$ (`MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) B`), let $L$ be a commutative ring and a $B$-algebra, and let $\pi : B[\![x_1,x_2]\!] \to L$ be a surjective $B$-algebra homomorphism whose kernel is exactly $I$, such that each $\pi(X_i)$ is nilpotent and such that $\pi$ is computed by evaluation at the point $(\pi(X_1),\pi(X_2))$: for every $G$, $\pi G =$ [`MvFormalGroup.adicEval`](def/MvFormalGroup_PointsV2.html#L20) of $G$ taken with respect to the zero ideal of $L$ at that point, where `adicEval J x` denotes `MvPowerSeries.eval₂ (algebraMap B L) x` formed using the discrete uniformity on the coefficients and the $J$-adic topology on the target. Let $G$ be a power series in two blocks of two variables, i.e. an element of `MvPowerSeries (Fin 2 ⊕ Fin 2) B`, and assume that for every natural number $n$ the evaluation of $G$, in the sense of `adicEval` with respect to the zero ideal of $\bigl(B[\![x_1,x_2]\!]/(X_1,X_2)^{n+1}\bigr) \otimes_B L$, at the point sending the variables of the first block to $\bar X_j \otimes 1$ and those of the second block to $1 \otimes \pi(X_j)$, is zero. Then $G$ lies in the ideal of $B[\![x_1,x_2,y_1,y_2]\!]$ generated by the image of $I$ under the substitution $X_l \mapsto X_{\mathrm{inr}\, l}$, that is, by the elements $f(y_1,y_2)$ for $f \in I$.
--
--   This is the one-sided bridge lemma converting the vanishing of a two-block power series at the points $(\bar x \otimes 1, 1 \otimes \pi x)$ of all finite truncations into membership in the ideal generated by $I$ in the second block of variables, the finite generation of $I$ being what makes the regrouping of coefficients legitimate. It is used in the analysis of formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-modules, where $L$ arises as the coordinate ring of an infinitesimal subgroup cut out by $I$, and is cited by [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.eq_span_setOf_invariant_of_subgroup_ideal_of_free`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.eq_span_setOf_invariant_of_subgroup_ideal_of_free).
